    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d256">

                <pb facs="0350" n="238" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg238"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/611: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-01-13T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 13,
                                1919, 4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>4037. Repeat to Paris and Rome. Am[erican] mission being advised direct.
                    Referring to Department’s No. 3991, Jan. 10 [<hi rendition="#italic">9</hi>], 7
                        p.m.<anchor n="33" xml:id="d256-f1"/> Following telegram from Ambassador
                    Morris at Tokio, January 9, 12 midnight, gives final status of railway
                    negotiations. The Department is authorizing Mr. Morris to proceed to Vladivostok
                    in the near future to settle preliminary arrangements and has told him that he
                    and Stevens can go ahead with the plan as soon as we notify him that Japanese
                    Ambassador at Washington has presented the matter formally to this Government,
                    at which time we will also instruct you to give formal notification to the
                    government to which you are accredited. In the meanwhile please keep the
                    government to which you are accredited fully advised, orally, of the status of
                    the situation to date.</p>
                <p>[Here follows text of telegram from the Ambassador in Japan, January 9, 12
                    midnight, with final sentence omitted, printed <hi rendition="#italic"
                    >ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg236">p. 236</ref>.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d256-f1" n="33" xml:id="d256-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it communicated the text of telegram from the Ambassador in Japan,
                    Dec. 27, 1918, 10 p.m. (<ref target="frus1918Russiav03#pg_301"><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1918, Russia, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">iii</hi>, p. 301</ref>), which telegram
                    contained the text of railway plan printed <hi rendition="#italic"
                    >infra.</hi></p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
